    "notes": "Real captured 2026-08-12 restart-storm day: ONE continuous physical drying draw (12:53-14:25 main cycle, then the anti-crease/keep-fresh tail through ~16:11) that the LIVE (legacy) dryer_monitor.py published as FOUR separate Running blocks, because three unrelated whole-installation dropouts (door sensor unavailable-> unknown->off blips at 13:25, 14:47, 15:33 - the ESPHome/HA reconnect signature) each coincided with an app re-initialization that could not corroborate the in-progress Running state and fell through to Off (spec F2/4.3: a helper-only or unclear restore has no clock and falls through to Off), only to re-confirm Running within 60-170s once a live power sample crossed start_w again. This is exactly the F2 restore-corroboration gap the new engine's hypothesis/corroboration logic (spec 8) is designed to close - this tape pins what the OLD app actually did, as the differential-oracle baseline, NOT a target the new engine must reproduce. The final Off at 16:12:30.996 is NOT a restart (no dropout signature): the door opened (16:12:30.255) about 42s after power finally settled for good, and the legacy app never published Unemptied/Emptied for this cycle - it went straight Running->Off, consistent with its low-power finish-confirm not yet having fired before the door-open was seen (RUNNING+DOOR_OPENED+low-power+fill_window -> OFF, the add-laundry/interrupt route in the dryer transition table, spec 4). announced/pushed/hypothesis are NOT asserted per-entry: only sensor.dryer_state's published value was captured, not the live app's notification log."
